<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#silk-road">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Silk Road</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">Silk</a> Road was the network of overland trade routes linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. Along it travelled silk, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a>, horses, precious metals, religions and technologies. Empires including the Han and Tang dynasties, the Parthian and Sasanian empires and the Mongol, Chagatai and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> states drew wealth from controlling its routes.</p></div>
